{
  "title": "Fat Embolism Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9055/fat-embolism-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 2 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fat Embolism Syndrome is an acute respiratory disorder caused by an inflammatory response to embolized fat globules that may enter the bloodstream as a result of acute long bone fractures or intramedullary instrumentation. Patients present with hypoxia, changes in mental status, and petechial rash.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with presence of hypoxemia (PaO2 < 60), CNS depression, petechial rash, and pulmonary edema.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is focused on prevention with early stabilization of long bone fractures. Mechanical ventilation with high levels of PEEP is the recommended treatment for acute presentation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3-4% with isolated long bone trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "10-15% with polytrauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fat and marrow elements are embolized into the bloodstream during",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acute long bone fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "intramedullary instrumentation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**intramedullary nailing**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**hip & knee arthroplasty**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathophysiology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "two theories regarding the causes of fat embolism include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**mechanical theory**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "embolism is caused by droplets of bone marrow fat released into venous system",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**biochemical theory**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "lipoprotein lipase induces free fatty acid production with resultant hyperinflammatory response similar to ARDS",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diagnosis Criteria",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Major (1)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**hypoxemia (PaO2 < 60)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**CNS depression (changes in mental status)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**petechial rash**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pulmonary edema",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Minor (4)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**tachycardia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pyrexia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "retinal emboli",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fat in urine or sputum",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "thrombocytopenia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased HCT",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
